                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to boxing or fighting with fists."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ccd86f64-b571-49e5-944f-3cca7555409d",
                                "sense_id": "1029d3ae-5a18-38c5-ae11-3781795b58bc",
                                "text": "But she was here interrupted […] by her father's hat being heavily flung from his hand and striking her face. Accustomed to such occasional manifestations of his sense of parental duty, Pleasant merely wiped her face on her hair (which of course had tumbled down) before she twisted it up. This was another common procedure on the part of the ladies of the Hole, when heated by verbal or fistic altercation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ed2515f-5dda-4447-854c-9dc847fb1e74",
                                "sense_id": "1029d3ae-5a18-38c5-ae11-3781795b58bc",
                                "text": "The fight over this ordinance had as one of its features, a few days ago, a fistic encounter between Robert Oestermaier and Attorney Curtis M. Willock."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b5a6a80-499b-4e09-b52f-c20e8c624041",
                                "sense_id": "1029d3ae-5a18-38c5-ae11-3781795b58bc",
                                "text": "The Englishman, whose right eye was nearly closed, took his corner where he was liberally drenched with water and when the bell went came on gamey and brimful of pluck, confident of knocking out the fistic Eblanite in jigtime."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e4c370b-4dc8-4721-9227-a92add0e0259",
                                "sense_id": "1029d3ae-5a18-38c5-ae11-3781795b58bc",
                                "text": "Though analyst Gary Galley first said the fistic defeat would probably spell the end for Pittsburgh, he later agreed with his colleagues that Talbot's impression of a punching bag had indeed changed the course of the game."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
